 *   **Time Complexity:** The 3D forward FFT is performed only once [S1, S2]. For each view, the modification of $H$ to $H'$ is a 2D operation on the slice plane. The cost of recomputing $H'$ is negligible compared to the cost of interpolation itself, because the support of $H$ is small ($3^3$ to $5^3$) and $D(s)$ is simple [S1, S2].
 *   **Memory Complexity:** Requires storage for the 3D spectrum $F(s)$ and the filter $H(s)$. No additional volume copies are needed [S1, S2].
