 ## Background
-*   **Origin:** Developed by Takashi Totsuka and Marc Levoy in 1993 [S2, S3, S4].
-*   **Development:** It extends the Frequency Domain Volume Rendering algorithm by incorporating depth cueing and directional shading entirely in the frequency domain, using properties of the Fourier transform (differentiation theorem) to avoid spatial domain multiplication [S1, S2].
-*   **Usage:** Used in fast volume rendering applications where depth cues are important for shape perception, such as medical imaging and scientific visualization [S2].
